for this PR I wanted to limit the scope to the re-authentication (_in case user changed credentials_)

on the other hand, I already thinking about a re-configuration flow (_change hostname/ip, port, ssl, ..._), but still struggle with, how to consider the NAS is not reachable, since settings were changed or it is only rebooting :thinking: 
For now I see these options:
- user can simple add the same NAS again (_identified via its serial_), the configflow will recognize this and update the already existing config-entry
- the settings host/ip, port and ssl will be available to be changed via the options-flow

@balloob what do you think? Do I miss here any already existing approach to handle re-configurations of - let's say - basic settings?
